  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.switchByGen[0].highBeam": "Left-hand steering column stalk: push forward = high beam; pull toward you = high beam flasher (overtaking signal). The turn signals are on the same stalk. To change lanes, hold the stalk at the pressure point; this generation has no one-touch three-flash function",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.switchByGen[0].fog": "Pull the light switch out to the first detent = front fog lamps (green LED on the knob lights up); pull further to the second detent = rear fog lamp added (yellow LED lights up)",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.switchByGen[0].drl": "No separate daytime running light switch; a permanent-on mode can be set in the multifunction display menu",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.switchByGen[0].notes": "Headlamp range is set with a manual knob (three positions 0/1/2, according to front and rear occupancy and luggage load); the headlamp delay switch-off can be set in stages from 0 to 60 seconds in the menu; the locator lighting (parking lights/tail lights/licence plate lamp on when unlocking) can be switched in the same menu",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.switchByGen[1].verified": "Verified (illustration in the official W204 English owner's manual)",
