  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.switchByGen[1].highBeam": "Combination switch: push forward = high beam (K indicator in the instrument cluster lights up), returns to off when released; pull toward you = high beam flasher. The combination switch also operates the turn signals",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.switchByGen[1].fog": "With the switch at low beam (L) or AUTO (c), press button N on the light switch panel = front fog lamps, and the green N indicator in the instrument cluster lights up. The button type and indicator colour for the rear fog lamp were not verified",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.switchByGen[1].drl": "The daytime running lights can be switched on and off in the onboard computer; the manual also notes that legislation in some countries requires lights during the day",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.switchByGen[1].notes": "Interior lighting: buttons in the front overhead panel — c = front interior lighting, u = rear interior lighting, p = reading lamps, | = automatic interior lighting control; the emergency lighting comes on automatically after a collision and can be switched off with the hazard warning button. Headlamp cleaning: with the lights on and the engine running, the headlamps are cleaned automatically after ten wipe cycles with washer fluid",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.switchByGen[2].verified": "Not verified — the official online manual is a JS-rendered page, so only section headings could be retrieved",
