  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.switchByGen[3].location": "The official manual groups light operation into a single section, \"Exterior lighting — Operating the combination switch for the light\", unlike W205, which has a separate \"Light switch\" section — the direction of this supports the light control having been integrated into the left-hand combination switch, but whether it is a rotating collar on the stalk or a button at the end of the stalk could not be verified",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.switchByGen[3].notes": "For this generation too we could not obtain a reliable source for the exact operation, so it is left blank rather than guessed. Please refer to the owner's manual supplied with your car",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.parkingLight.what": "The parking light (Standlicht / parking light / standing lamp) lights only the front and rear lamps on one side while the car is parked at the roadside. Its purpose is to show the width of the car on unlit roads while drawing only a very small current, so that the battery does not run flat.",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.parkingLight.diffFromPosition": "Parking lamps (side lights) light both sides at once and mark the whole vehicle during short stops at night; the standing lamp lights the front and rear lamps on one side only, so that when parking on the road side only that edge is marked. On the W204 light knob these are different positions: T lights the parking lamps on both sides, W / X light one side.",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.parkingLight.steps[0]": "Bring the car to a stop.",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.parkingLight.steps[1]": "Locate the light switch — on both W203 and W204 it is a rotary knob on the left of the dashboard.",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.parkingLight.steps[2]": "W204: turn the knob to W for the left side only, or to X for the right side only. The official manual illustration reads: \"1 W Left-hand standing lamps, 2 X Right-hand standing lamps, 3 T Parking lamps, license plate and instrument lighting\".",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.parkingLight.steps[3]": "W203: the knob likewise has two separate positions, \"Parking lights, left\" and \"Parking lights, right\"; turn to the relevant position to light one side only.",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.parkingLight.steps[4]": "Just lock the car and walk away — the lamps stay on; turn the knob back to off when you return to switch them off.",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.parkingLight.correction": "A widely repeated owner tip says that \"after switching off the ignition you can move the turn signal stalk to one side to light the parking light on that side\" — no such procedure appears in the W203 or W204 official manuals we retrieved; on both generations it is a separate position on the light knob. (W205 / W206 could not be verified; later models may have changed to a different method.)",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.parkingLight.when": "Parking at the roadside at night (when parking on the right, light the left side so that oncoming traffic sees the left edge of the car), giving way on narrow roads, and short stops on unlit roads. Legislation in some European countries requires the road-side lamps to be lit when parking at night.",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.parkingLight.notes": "The parking light draws very little current, but leaving it on for a whole night or longer can still affect the battery; on older cars with a weak battery, avoid leaving it on for long periods.",
  "CONTROL_DATA.lighting.lampsLocation[0].name": "Side light (parking lamp)",
