  "CONTROL_DATA.special[0].system": "SBC Sensotronic Brake Control",
  "CONTROL_DATA.special[0].models": "Fitted only to models with an electrohydraulic brake system, such as W211 (E-Class), W219 (CLS) and R230 (SL). The HELLA technical bulletin limits the scope explicitly to \"Model series 211, 219 and 230\", and our research found no evidence of any W203/S203 with SBC — so the conclusion is: the C-Class (including the estate) has no SBC. If you see an SBC-related fault message, you are looking at E-Class or SL material.",
  "CONTROL_DATA.special[0].symptom": "The instrument cluster shows a message such as \"Service Brake! Visit workshop\", brake assistance is reduced and the braking distance becomes longer",
  "CONTROL_DATA.special[0].action": "If this message appears, have the SBC pump and pressure accumulator checked at an authorised workshop immediately and do not keep driving for long; after repair the SBC counter must be reset with a diagnostic tester. Do not remove or install high-pressure components yourself.",
  "CONTROL_DATA.special[1].system": "AIRMATIC air suspension",
  "CONTROL_DATA.special[1].models": "Optional on W205 (including C350e, C43 etc.) and optional on W206. Which variants have air suspension varies by market and has not been verified one by one here; W203/S204 use conventional steel springs and have no air suspension.",
  "CONTROL_DATA.special[1].symptom": "Abnormal ride height, one side sagging, and suspension fault messages in the instrument cluster",
  "CONTROL_DATA.special[1].action": "If the body clearly sinks or you hear noises, avoid high speeds and have the car inspected nearby (check the air springs and air lines for leaks, the compressor and the level sensors). Such faults must be diagnosed on the individual car before a price can be quoted; there is no universal price.",
